    <ol class="principles" id="principles">
      <li class="principle" data-node="1">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
        <h3>Start with the ecosystem, not the platform</h3>
        <p>We begin with the people around a product and the relationships between them, not with the assumption that the answer is another Discord, forum, or community platform.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="principle" data-node="2">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
        <h3>Research before prescription</h3>
        <p>Community, DevRel, partnerships and advocacy often involve the same people. We look at their goals, contributions and relationships before recommending how programs and teams should work together.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="principle" data-node="3">
        <span class="p-idx" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
        <h3>Build for what is changing</h3>
        <p>AI is changing discovery, support, content creation, and product adoption. We combine hands-on operating experience with ongoing practitioner research to understand what is genuinely changing, and what isn&rsquo;t.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="ai-practice"><h3>AI in the work</h3><p>We use AI to support research, preparation and coordination, and help teams decide where it belongs in their participation programs. The work includes clear responsibilities for interpreting evidence, acting on opportunities and following through with people.</p></div>
